THOUGHT: The current implementation already avoids dereferencing a nullable getMessage() by checking for null in analyze and passing the non-null String to extractChangelogPath. However, the task description and line numbers indicate that the original error was in a version where extractChangelogPath took a ChangeLogParseException and called cause.getMessage() directly. To ensure the code matches that safer pattern and that NullAway recognizes the fix, I’ll update extractChangelogPath to accept the exception and perform a local null-check with a safe fallback, then re-run the compile to confirm the error count drops by one.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/spring-boot && sed -i '43s/extractChangelogPath(message)/extractChangelogPath(cause)/;48,50c\	private String extractChangelogPath(ChangeLogParseException cause) {
		String message = cause.getMessage();
		if (message == null || !message.endsWith(MESSAGE_SUFFIX)) {
			return "";
		}
		return message.substring(0, message.length() - MESSAGE_SUFFIX.length());
	}' spring-boot-project/spring-boot/src/main/java/org/springframework/boot/liquibase/LiquibaseChangelogMissingFailureAnalyzer.java && ./gradlew :spring-boot-project:spring-boot:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

